# Proofread-only copy (`projects.ts`)

When changing **`Project`** strings ( **`description`**, **`intro`**, **`role`**, section **`text`**, media **`label`**, etc.) in [`src/data/projects.ts`](src/data/projects.ts):

## Allowed (objective fixes only)

- Clear **spelling** mistakes.
- Clear **grammar** errors in standard English **without** altering meaning (e.g. agreement, a clearly missing article).
- **Punctuation** that repairs broken sentences when structure stays the same (periods, stray double spaces).
- **Obvious typos** in proper nouns when the intended spelling is clear from context.

## Not allowed without explicit user approval

- Rephrasing, tightening, or “smoothing” for style.
- Synonym swaps (“nine” ↔ “9”, US ↔ UK spelling) unless the user asks.
- Restructuring (splitting/merging paragraphs, reordering clauses).
- Voice changes (e.g. removing informal openers like “Ah,”).

If a line could be **intentional voice** vs. an error, **leave it** or ask the user before editing.

## Figma

Treat Figma exports as **structure and hierarchy** reference. Final strings should match **user-approved copy**, not automatic paraphrase from design tools.
